{"id":18199,"name":"Eaton County","slug":"eaton-county","state":"Michigan","code":"MI","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/michigan-tax-deed-sales-property-deals-90-off/eaton-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-07-20T14:50:32","facts":{"taxSaleType":"Tax Deed Sale","typicalSaleDate":"October","bidProcedure":"Premium Bid","deposit":"$1,000.00","registration":"Pre-register online or on-site by noon with $1,000 deposit","extra":[{"label":"Sale Contact","value":"Eaton County Treasurer’s Office"},{"label":"Auction Site","value":"BippusUSA.com"},{"label":"County Website","value":"Eaton County Official Website"},{"label":"Payment","value":"Full payment due shortly after auction ends; includes 10% buyer’s premium and deed preparation fee. Cash or certified check preferred; personal checks need to clear."},{"label":"Deed Issuance","value":"Quit Claim Deed issued within 30 days"},{"label":"Liens","value":"All prior liens except IRS and certain environmental liens are canceled"},{"label":"Property Research","value":"Buyers should conduct thorough research on property conditions and any legal compliance requirements"}]},"bodyHtml":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"Am1607qfCYmw3uoWMZJJNfCOkO029aUgXFQyBG3L7tyh6TjiSeP8D1RFxizxrnjau4pvNv95RYtKEKW2GMddQEolqhb5DIs\"><iframe title=\"Unlock Extraordinary Up to 90% Property Discounts - Eaton County - Michigan Tax Deed Investing\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/3gW_-TD6Dsk?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Unlock-Extraordinary-Up-to-90%-Property-Discounts---Eaton-County---Michigan-Tax-Deed-Investing\">Unlock Extraordinary Property Discounts of Up to 90% in Eaton County, MI</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Buying properties at Eaton County, <a href=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-deed/tax-deed-states/michigan-tax-deed-sales-property-deals-90-off/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Michigan&#8217;s</mark></a> tax foreclosure sale lets you acquire properties at 40 to 90 percent off. Here&#8217;s a quick guide to help you navigate this opportunity.</p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"How-to-Participate-in-the-Auction\">How to Participate in the Auction</h4>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"1\" class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Register Early:</strong> You can pre-register online at <a href=\"http://www.bippususa.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">BippusUSA.com</mark></a> or show up by noon on sale day with a $1,000 deposit.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Check Tax Status:</strong> Ensure you have no outstanding property taxes in Eaton County to get your bid card.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Prepare to Bid:</strong> Foreclosed properties are auctioned due to tax non-payment. However, the county may pull properties before the sale.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Understanding-the-Auction-Process\">Understanding the Auction Process</h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>First Round:</strong> The auctioneer sets minimum bids for properties, covering all back taxes and costs. The highest bidder wins.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Subsequent Rounds:</strong> The auctioneer may auction unsold properties again with potentially lower minimum bids.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Winning-the-Bid\">Winning the Bid</h4>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Payment:</strong> If you win, pay quickly. You must make full payment, including a 10% buyer’s premium and a deed preparation fee. You can use cash, certified check, or personal check (subject to clearance).</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Deed Issuance:</strong> You’ll receive a Quit Claim Deed within 30 days, but you must handle any current year’s taxes and fees.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>As-Is Purchase:</strong> Properties are sold &#8220;as is,&#8221; so it&#8217;s crucial to research thoroughly.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Important-Details-for-Eaton-County-Tax-Deed-Sales\">Important Details for Eaton County Tax Deed Sales</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>For more information, visit the <a href=\"https://www.eatoncounty.org/301/Treasurer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Eaton County Treasurer&#8217;s page</mark></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse-296x197.webp 296w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse-768x512.webp 768w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse-20x13.webp 20w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse-32x21.webp 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" type=\"image/webp\"><img src=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse.png\" height=\"720\" width=\"1081\" srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse.png 1081w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse-541x360.png 541w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse-296x197.png 296w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse-768x512.png 768w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse-20x13.png 20w, https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Eaton-County-Michigan-Courthouse-32x21.png 32w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1081px) 100vw, 1081px\" class=\"wp-image-18208 sp-no-webp\" alt=\"Eaton County Michigan Courthouse\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"  > </picture></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Book a Call with Dustin Hahn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Frequently-Asked-Questions\">Frequently Asked Questions</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: What happens if I don&#8217;t pay my bid on time?</strong> <br>A: If you fail to pay your bid on time, you will lose your deposit, and the auctioneer will offer the property to the next highest bidder or re-auction it.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: Are there any properties I should avoid?</strong> <br>A: It&#8217;s essential to do your homework. Avoid properties with unresolved environmental liens or significant structural issues.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Q: Can I get financing for these properties?</strong> <br>A: Typically, these auctions require immediate payment, so traditional financing options may not be available. Be prepared to pay in cash or certified funds.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>For more detailed guidance, check out the <a href=\"https://www.tax-sale.info/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Michigan Public Land Auction site</mark></a> and the <a href=\"https://www.michigan.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">State of Michigan’s tax foreclosure information</mark></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Useful-Links\">Useful Links</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://online.flippingbook.com/view/249551426/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Eaton County Tax Deed Information</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.eatoncounty.org/301/Treasurer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Eaton County Treasurer</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"http://www.bippususa.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-bl